      "comment": "Fork identifiers for Holesky, a proof-of-stake testnet that was NEVER proof-of-work. Its terminal total difficulty is exactly zero, which the reference client reads as merged at genesis.",
      "thisNetworkHasZeroBlockBasedBoundaries": "Every fork here is a timestamp. Ethereum mainnet is block-based then timestamp-based, Sepolia has exactly one block boundary and it is the Merge, and Ethereum Classic is block-based throughout with no timestamp fork at all. This is the fourth shape and the simplest: a schedule with no block dimension whatsoever.",
      "mergedAtGenesisIsTheTHIRDBranch": "../sepolia/consensus/ records the three-way predicate the client uses for post-merge status. Holesky answers through the branch neither mainnet nor Sepolia uses: a terminal total difficulty of exactly zero. There was no proof-of-work phase to end.",
